# Every CSV is LF in the repository and in checkouts. Python's csv module
# defaults to CRLF, so each writer passes lineterminator="\n" as well; the
# pre-commit csv-lf hook blocks a CSV that reintroduces CR bytes.
*.csv text eol=lf

# Generated outputs: regenerated by scripts/build_seed_outputs.py and committed
# because the pages fetch them. A three-way merge of two regenerations splices
# files neither run produced, so git must not merge them: it keeps our side and
# flags the path. Resolve by rerunning `python scripts/build_seed_outputs.py`
# on the merged seeds. (Same rule as pricephillips/data-center-map.)
#
# Not listed on purpose: seeds, review files and data/snapshots/manifest.csv
# are sources of record or append-only, where a normal merge is correct.
data/processed/** -merge
docs/coverage_audit.md -merge
